 "text": "9/29/26, 10:15 AM\ne That dunning groups are excluded from dunning if the open percentage portion of the items assigned is less than a specific\nlimit percentage rate\n\nDunning Activities\n\nDefinition\n\nMeasure taken when a specific dunning level of a dunning procedure is reached.\n\nStructure\n\nYou define dunning activities in the Customizing activity Configure Dunning Activities by specifying a function module with a\npredefined interface. For the dunning activity key, specify the name of the dunning activity, the activity type, and the name of the\nfunction module that executes the dunning activity. For activities that support the printing of Print Workbench forms, you have to\ndefine an application form.\n\n1 Note\nNote that the function modules for dunning activities for correspondence dunning use a different interface than the function\nmodules for dunning activities for dunning open items.\n\nThen assign the dunning activities to the dunning levels of a dunning procedure in the activity Configure Dunning Procedure. You\ncan assign a dunning activity to different dunning levels of different dunning procedures as well assigning different dunning\nactivities to one dunning level.\n\nWhen you execute the dunning activity run, the function modules defined for the activities for a dunning level are called up.\n\nDunning activities are industry-specific. However, you can also define installation-specific activities.\n\nee Example\nPossible dunning activities are:\ne Creation of a dunning letter\ne Creation of a note by a clerk\ne Submission of items to a collection agency\ne Termination of a contract\ne Setting a lock\ne Creation of collection work items\n\ne Disconnection of a Service\n\nDunning Grouping\n",
